## island-io/mila (Apache License 2.0)

- Source: https://github.com/island-io/mila
- Originally developed by Uri Harduf at Island Technology, Inc.

The speaker-diarization integration in
`src/lib/extraction/transcription/diarize.py` ports, from Mila:

- the offline pyannote.audio SpeakerDiarization pipeline configuration
  (segmentation-3.0 + wespeaker-voxceleb-resnet34-LM, clustering params),
- the pyannote 3.x compatibility monkey-patches (torch.load weights_only;
  speechbrain LazyModule), and
- the path-substring model-directory naming required to route the embedding
  to the torch backend.

Mila itself builds on ivrit.ai Whisper finetunes (Hebrew), whisper.cpp (MIT)
for local inference, OpenAI Whisper model weights, and pyannote.audio for
speaker diarization.

